From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jens Willmer <info@jwillmer.de>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 11:14:41 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 38/43] minimize: options file to turn off the second line and
 the hover preview

For narrow panels (cosmic-applets#297): `~/.config/minimize-ws/options`
takes `second_line = true|false` and `hover_preview = true|false`, both
on by default, re-read on change like the other config files.

Without the second line every item shows its title on one line, centred
like a short title; a tab count (Firefox, terminal, Files) moves before
the title as "(n) ", media, launcher and title parts are dropped.

Without the hover preview no item opens the preview popup, also in the
overflow popup, and nothing is captured for it: no live capture, and no
thumbnails on a top or bottom panel. Click, middle click and the window
menu are unchanged.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

